##DESCRIPTION
##   This problem asks a student to switch a confindence interval to plus/minus form.
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Confidence intervals)
## DBsection(Concepts)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Jessie Oehrlein)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('confidence interval')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

$lb = random(13,15,.01);
$ub = random(20,22,.01);

$me = .5*($ub - $lb);
$pe = .5*($ub + $lb);

BEGIN_PGML
Suppose you have an interval of [`([$lb], [$ub])`]. Rewrite this interval in plus/minus form. Do not round. 

  [_]{$pe} [`\pm`] [_]{$me}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
To switch from an interval to plus/minus form, first find the midpoint/average of the endpoints or [`` \frac{[$lb]+[$ub]}{2} = [$pe]``]. 

Next, the plus/minus term is half the range of the interval or [``  \frac{[$ub]-[$lb]}{2} = [$me]``].

This can then be written as [`` [$pe] \pm [$me] ``]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.